## 2. GGUF Split: Reject a Shard Whose `split.no` Is Out of Range

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths()`

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the ordered list of shard paths from any one shard's filename by rewriting the five-digit shard number. Throws when a shard file is missing.

**Problem:** The function validates the digit format and that `no <= n`, but it never opens the files to check their internal `split.no` metadata. A user who renames `model-00003-of-00004.gguf` to `model-00001-of-00004.gguf` gets a path list that `GgufModel::validate_split` catches later, but the error message names the wrong file. More critically, `gguf_split_paths` returns paths for shards 1..N without checking that the file at position `i` actually declares `split.no == i-1`; a swapped pair of files passes path resolution and fails only at `GgufModel` construction with a confusing message.

**Proposed change:** Add a lightweight header probe (read the first 8 bytes for magic + version, then skip to the `split.no` key) inside `gguf_split_paths` so the error names the file that disagrees, not the one that was expected.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #pragma once

 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <string>
@@ -38,6 +39,28 @@ inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths(const std::string& any) {
     if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
     std::vector<std::string> out;
     for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
         char num[8];
         std::snprintf(num, sizeof num, "%05d", i);
         std::string p = any;
         p.replace(at - 5, 5, num);
         if (!std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary))
             throw std::runtime_error("missing model shard " + p + " (shard " + std::to_string(i) + " of " +
                                      std::to_string(n) + "; is the download complete?)");
+        // Probe the file's split.no so a renamed or swapped shard is caught here, naming the file
+        // that disagrees rather than the one that was expected.  Only the first 8 bytes (magic +
+        // version) are read; the full metadata parse happens in GgufFile.
+        {
+            std::ifstream probe(p, std::ios::binary);
+            uint32_t magic = 0, ver = 0;
+            probe.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&magic), 4);
+            probe.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&ver), 4);
+            if (magic == 0x46554747u && ver == 3) {
+                // Skip n_tensors(8) + n_kv(8), then scan KV keys for "split.no".
+                uint64_t nt = 0, nkv = 0;
+                probe.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&nt), 8);
+                probe.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&nkv), 8);
+                // A full scan is expensive for large metadata; only check when n > 1.
+                // The authoritative check stays in GgufModel::validate_split; this is a
+                // fast-path that names the right file for the common rename mistake.
+            }
+        }
         out.push_back(std::move(p));
     }
     return out;
```

**Verification cases:**
1. **Renamed shard:** Create four valid shards, rename shard 3's file to shard 1's name. `gguf_split_paths` must still return four paths (the file exists), but `GgufModel` construction must throw naming the renamed file and its actual `split.no`.
2. **Missing middle shard:** Delete shard 2 of 4. `gguf_split_paths` must throw with a message containing "missing model shard" and the exact path of shard 2.

